[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged on subject lines ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject))
and marked known as one parser bug. Read by tenant and channel, its reports are two
problems. Each now has its own ticket.

<Callout kind="warn">
The parser fix queued for #4471 does not close the hint problem.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

## The two problems

- **`parser`**: the shared parser reads every date month first. A day-first tenant's dates
  come out with day and month swapped, on every channel and both booking forms.
- **`hint`**: `booking-v3` prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People at day-first
  tenants type what the hint says, and the form reads it day first. Only reports sent through the
  form, only at tenants on `booking-v3`. The parser fix leaves this as it is; the hint has to
  change.

## For the desk

- Intake's `intakeTag` is a guess from the reporter's browser. File by tenant and channel
  (`#lib/kb/causes.ts`), not by the tag.
- Same subject does not mean same problem: both share subjects like "Wrong day on the invite".
- Reports the desk read as a one-day move (`desk-notes.json`) stay under their tenant's cause.

